text:
Data
Both datasets come from Basketball-Reference for the 2025-26 regular season: the league-wide advanced stats page, and the salary table on each of the 30 team pages. The site’s robots.txt allows these pages and sets a three-second crawl delay, and Sports Reference blocks clients sending more than 20 requests a minute, so the scraper waits four seconds between each of its 32 requests. No login or paywall is involved.

adv_raw &lt;- read_html(paste0(base_url, "/leagues/NBA_2026_advanced.html")) |&gt;
  html_element("table") |&gt;
  html_table()

for (tm in teams) {
  salary_list[[tm]] &lt;- scrape_team_salary(tm)  # salary table sits inside an HTML comment
  Sys.sleep(4)
}

Cleaning took more work than scraping. Traded players appear once per team plus a combined row, and I kept the combined row. Names don’t always match across pages: suffixes like “Jr.” appear on one page but not the other, and in one case a Cyrillic letter looks identical to a Latin one. Players were matched on a normalised name key, with two remaining cases fixed by hand. Players on two-way contracts have no listed salary and drop out. Keeping players with at least 1,000 minutes leaves 278.

Explore the map
The interactive map below lets you switch between median income, the poverty rate, and the local clusters. Click any tract to see its figures.


Code
cl_cols &lt;- c("High-income cluster"        = "#B2182B",
             "Low-income cluster"         = "#2166AC",
             "High tract, low neighbours" = "#F4A582",
             "Low tract, high neighbours" = "#92C5DE",
             "Not significant"            = "#E0E0E0")

pal_inc &lt;- colorNumeric("viridis", log10(tracts$med_inc))
pal_pov &lt;- colorNumeric("OrRd", tracts$pov_rate, na.color = "#dddddd")
pal_cl  &lt;- colorFactor(unname(cl_cols), levels = names(cl_cols))

popup &lt;- sprintf(
  "&lt;b&gt;%s&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Median household income: %s&lt;br&gt;Poverty rate: %.1f%%&lt;br&gt;
   Bachelor's or higher: %.1f%%&lt;br&gt;Rent-burdened renters: %.1f%%&lt;br&gt;
   Distance to City Hall: %.1f mi&lt;br&gt;Cluster: %s",
  sub(";.*", "", tracts$NAME), dollar(tracts$med_inc), tracts$pov_rate,
  tracts$ba_share, tracts$rent_burden, tracts$dist_mi, tracts$cluster)

add_layer &lt;- function(map, group, fill) {
  addPolygons(map, group = group, fillColor = fill, fillOpacity = 0.75,
              weight = 0.4, color = "white", popup = popup,
              highlightOptions = highlightOptions(weight = 2, color = "black",
                                                  bringToFront = TRUE))
}

leaflet(tracts, height = 600) |&gt;
  addProviderTiles(providers$CartoDB.Positron) |&gt;
  add_layer("Median income", ~pal_inc(log10(med_inc))) |&gt;
  add_layer("Poverty rate", ~pal_pov(pov_rate)) |&gt;
  add_layer("Income clusters", ~pal_cl(cluster)) |&gt;
  addMarkers(lng = -75.1636, lat = 39.9524, label = "City Hall") |&gt;
  addLayersControl(baseGroups = c("Median income", "Poverty rate", "Income clusters"),
                   options = layersControlOptions(collapsed = FALSE))
